Hey Maksim,

Thank you for raising this.

In step 5 for RH, there are two possible scenarios:

* Partial refund option is available → no need to mark the order fraudulent, no action is needed
* Partial refund option not available (anymore or at all) → mark the order fraudulent 

I have adjusted the steps a bit to make this more clear:

* {color:#36b37e}Go to the order page{color}
* {color:#36b37e}Scroll down and check if the partial refund option is available.{color}
** {color:#36b37e}If it is, there is no need to mark the order as fraudulent, proceed by replying to the user as advised below{color}
** {color:#36b37e}If it is not available or the order has already been refunded and you cannot see the refund option anymore, mark the payment as fraudulent.{color}
*** {color:#36b37e}In the {color}{color:#36b37e}_Mark payment as fraud_{color}{color:#36b37e} section, add a link to the Zendesk or Beehive ticket and click {color}{color:#36b37e}_Mark._ {color}{color:#36b37e}If a {color}{color:#36b37e}_server error (999)_{color}{color:#36b37e} is displayed, you may ignore it. There is no need to escalate the order to the Fraud team.{color}
* {color:#36b37e}Reply to the user that we have taken internal measures to solve this issue (do not disclose what exactly).{color}

In case you are worried that we are not taking proper action in certain scenarios, some context from our fraud team:

_Blocking users is not the best solution for these unknown charges cases. By blocking the user, we’re killing the user completely and hurting our GMV without need. The whole process of unknown charges is being re-vamped, waiting on our devs to be updated. Once it happens, you’ll be able to mark payments instead of orders, regardless of business lines. Marking payments will essentially kill the card, therefore, resolving the issue without hurting GMV from potentially good users that just had a case of a friendly chargeback. Until this happens, please just keep following the current article. The fraudsters will be stopped once payments turn bad._


Let us know if there is anything else we can help with.

Wishing you a lovely week\! 💫

