Hello Kadri\! 

It seems there has been a misunderstanding - during one of our UK OPS/HP syncs we discussed that your team would request for a new blocking option in Admin similarly to the {{High Priority Case}} block, so that the agents wouldn't have to manually enter the blocking message. This would also ensure that nobody outside of the agents that are handling safety events have access to remove the block.

Kam, during UK OPS/HP sync we discussed the possibility of getting this new blocking option and apply it globally. Are there still plans to go forward with this?

There are a couple of items that should be considered if you wish to start using the "Other" custom blocking message option instead: 

* With entering the blocking message and length of the block manually, this will leave room for manual errors;
* The rest of the company has access to remove and add this type of block (for example Operations), which means that anybody can remove the block. This, in return, would mean that you’d have to start conducting checks on these profiles to ensure that nobody outside of the team has removed this specific block from a user who is alleged to be a bad actor;
* If the agent does not change the length of the block to be infinite manually (Admin suggests 1 year as a standard), then after 1 year you’d have to start going over those same profiles and add a new block in case they still haven’t responded;
* If you were planning to filter these users in Admin by the blocking message and length of the block, due to manual errors, it will be a challenge to sort these out later on. 

Thank you

{quote}Could you tell me what the difference is between “Robbery blocking” and “User(s) blocking” in admin? So we can figure out which option would be best for us going forward.{quote}

Answer is in the content of my previous message (=

Robbery blocking = hard blocks the devices. Not only the user you block, but any user that shares the same devices won’t be able to log in. 

User(s) blocking = hard block the user + blacklist devices + blacklist cards. If the same device is used in another account, there won’t be an issue. 

{quote}Also, I noticed that neither of these options are available for this user, is that because we have completed a hard-block instead?{quote}

I believe so. But I already manually hard blocked the device. If you go to login accounts you’ll see that the device_uid is red, which means it’s hard blocked. Not sure if you have access, but you can see list of hard block devices here [https://admin.bolt.eu/user/DeviceBlacklist/|https://admin.bolt.eu/user/DeviceBlacklist/]

