the default (fraud side) config is used in quite narrow cases in RH:
1. if user has negative balance or bolt_credit is explicitly set as a payment method in the App (we don’t care what flow was used here).
2. if the above condition is true then: we do compare default config with pricing estimation price and choose the biggest number using the rule: (the idea for the rule was taken from payments system after simplifications back in summer 2021)

{noformat}if (pricingAmount >= amountRule.min_amount) {
  return Math.min(amountRule.max_amount, pricingAmount);
} else
  return amountRule.amount; // aka default amount from static config{noformat}

3. if #1 is false then we do fallback call to payments service (see [https://admin.prelive.bolt.eu/payment/DynamicConfigPaymentOrder|https://admin.prelive.bolt.eu/payment/DynamicConfigPaymentOrder])

