Hi [~accountid:609f85c547ba02006fe1b9c3] 

First, I should apologize for the delay\!
Actually, I missed your reply on 15th Dec and thought it’s still work in progress\!  

Please find the answers below (in purple):

_If a courier refers a new applicant and the new applicant becomes a Bolt courier and delivers X orders, both get some referral bonuses._ How does this referring work? Does it mean that the courier will enter the possible lead email/telephone number somewhere and an e-mail will go out to that person?
Or do couriers just know that they have a referral code to share and they choose how and where to share that?
{color:#6554c0}The latter one (couriers just know that they have a referral code to share and they choose how and where to share that). The existing couriers have their unique referral codes (e.g. email) and they can share it with anyone they want.{color} 
{color:#6554c0}Then,{color} {color:#6554c0}there is an optional field in the courier application forms. If a new applicant received a referral code, s/he can enter this code in the application form.{color}


Why would the referral code be the existing courier’s phone number or email? Can’t this referral code be just a generated code or a link (therefore not being their personal data?)

{color:#6554c0}Actually, having “email address” as the referral code is the simplest way to communicate this plan with couriers and track the result on our side. {color}
{color:#6554c0}To be more specific, we can generate a random code for each courier to be used as the referral code. But, the main issue is that local teams need to send specific comms to each courier to tell them about their referral code.{color}
{color:#6554c0}Also, with any new couriers joining the platform, they need to generate a new random number and send a customized message to these new joiners.{color}
{color:#6554c0}Besides, to track and analyze the data, local ops have to keep these random codes in a google-sheet since this data are not in the Admin.{color}

{color:#6554c0}To summarize, if there is a chance to use Email as the referral code, local teams prefer using it rather than creating random codes and doing extra efforts to maintain the process.{color}

Please let me know if you need more information.

Thank you so much\! :)

